  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "prose",
      "html": "<p>The Hebrew alphabet has 22 consonant letters. Five letters use a special shape at the end of a word, but these are positional variants rather than additional letters. Read each sign as a consonant and track the direction of the line from right to left. In a pointed text, vowel marks are written around these consonants without changing the consonantal alphabet itself.</p>"
